}:$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{{(5-(-5))}^{2}+{(3-(-3))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{136} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 34} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{34}}{2}=\\sqrt{34}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{34})^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-14793/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e75012ec-8203-574b-ba07-0a26e4cf4691"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-14793"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911/selection/cf87acaed38a457cd66a654ef6be886af905585d674b9ddca4b8a0d48d398a24" :answer/id #uuid "1f85e94e-18a9-59f6-a5ed-5b57945edba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=244" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911/selection/dfa4bfa952992edce8b2a6b58b5cfc2e575b02dd54479cb31c686e0c3037f483" :answer/id #uuid "a65ae077-05ba-53ca-8e1f-e2dac2366304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{61}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911/selection/48bb08aab597b383d40d5ae344fbd47340b93871a29dff007d83365873fa9cc9" :answer/id #uuid "5b4e850b-7f62-5ba1-9827-844c782a4369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=61" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911/selection/cf8fe844a52801017695ca454b5721ec09ce81e6a0c7a7f577256d02ece64ffb" :answer/id #uuid "56c88e1d-a5fa-5ef0-8cfd-40f60a27150b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=(61)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911/selection/aa24d208e1b617a5ceedd5e6cf319b4d221e3875fcbe99d5c13cda27ccd4d53b" :answer/id #uuid "d0c0a7b8-d3b2-59b7-b7d0-6376e1dca3b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=122" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "84d41c0e-8552-5118-bf3b-7ca2d5de6d3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-14911/selection/48bb08aab597b383d40d5ae344fbd47340b93871a29dff007d83365873fa9cc9" :answer-field/choices ["q-14911/selection/cf87acaed38a457cd66a654ef6be886af905585d674b9ddca4b8a0d48d398a24" "q-14911/selection/dfa4bfa952992edce8b2a6b58b5cfc2e575b02dd54479cb31c686e0c3037f483" "q-14911/selection/48bb08aab597b383d40d5ae344fbd47340b93871a29dff007d83365873fa9cc9" "q-14911/selection/cf8fe844a52801017695ca454b5721ec09ce81e6a0c7a7f577256d02ece64ffb" "q-14911/selection/aa24d208e1b617a5ceedd5e6cf319b4d221e3875fcbe99d5c13cda27ccd4d53b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-14911" :question/id #uuid "d66c00a8-9a9a-5616-939e-722845cb2e8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-14911" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956996/assets/1023ca76971805ffc07c0397565723973a6a65359cade8d0bfbfa5a5b63f8a5c.png)\n\nGiven that the points $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(6,5)$ and $(-6,-5),$ respectively, are the endpoints of a diameter of a circle centered at the origin, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a circle with radius $r,$ centered at the origin, is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the length of the diameter $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{{(5-(-5))}^{2}+{(6-(-6))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{244} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 61} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{61}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a diameter, the radius is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{61}}{2}=\\sqrt{61}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{61})^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =61.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard